  "summary": "The identified studies apply Bayesian hierarchical models, described as multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling, to the task of predicting customer attrition. El-Sayed et al. (2021) [V0209] and Haddad et al. (2024) [V0212] report results on the ChurnBench and AgriSat-4 datasets, respectively, with the former achieving an AUROC of 0.65 and the latter reporting an MAE of 0.86. Fischer et al. (2022) [V0210] and Gupta et al. (2023) [V0211] also apply this method, reporting an F1 score of 0.72 on MetroFlow and an accuracy of 0.79 on Atlas-ICU. Additionally, Fischer et al. (2022) [V0204] apply a different method (decentralised training) to customer attrition, achieving an F1 of 0.64 on AgriSat-4.",
